{"title":"Dialysis Technician Roadmap","role":"Dialysis Technician","summary":"A Dialysis Technician is an allied healthcare professional who supports the delivery of dialysis treatment for patients with kidney failure. The role combines patient care, dialysis-machine operation, water-treatment systems, infection control, treatment monitoring, equipment maintenance, and emergency preparedness.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Dialysis Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Dialysis Technician is an allied healthcare professional who supports the delivery of dialysis treatment for patients with kidney failure. The role combines patient care, dialysis-machine operation, water-treatment systems, infection control, treatment monitoring, equipment maintenance, and emergency preparedness."},{"type":"p","text":"Core responsibilities may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparing dialysis machines and treatment stations"},{"text":"Performing pre-treatment equipment checks"},{"text":"Preparing patients for dialysis"},{"text":"Connecting and disconnecting dialysis circuits within defined scope"},{"text":"Monitoring vital signs and treatment parameters"},{"text":"Maintaining infection-control standards"},{"text":"Monitoring dialysis water quality"},{"text":"Responding to treatment-related emergencies"},{"text":"Maintaining treatment records"},{"text":"Cleaning and maintaining dialysis equipment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician works as part of a multidisciplinary renal-care team, typically alongside nephrologists, nurses, and other healthcare professionals. Exact clinical responsibilities vary according to institutional policies, qualification, and applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus","Career Outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, microbiology, renal-system fundamentals"},{"text":"Strong healthcare foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Dialysis principles, machines, procedures"},{"text":"Core technical competence"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Clinical dialysis + complications + water systems"},{"text":"Advanced practical exposure"}],[{"text":"Final Year"},{"text":"Hospital/renal-centre internship"},{"text":"Job-ready Dialysis Technician"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Routine dialysis support"},{"text":"Junior Dialysis Technician"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"Independent technical workflow"},{"text":"Senior Dialysis Technician"}],[{"text":"5+ Years"},{"text":"Unit coordination, QA, equipment"},{"text":"Lead/Chief Dialysis Technologist"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-Wise Learning Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical & Renal Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a strong understanding of the human body and kidney function."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Pharmacology fundamentals"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Basic patient care"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Renal anatomy and physiology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Kidney function"},{"text":"Fluid balance"},{"text":"Electrolyte balance"},{"text":"Acid-base balance"},{"text":"Blood pressure regulation"},{"text":"Waste-product removal"},{"text":"Acute kidney injury"},{"text":"Chronic kidney disease"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Target outcome","text":"Understand normal kidney function and what happens when renal function declines."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Dialysis Technology Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build technical knowledge of dialysis."},{"type":"h","text":"Hemodialysis fundamen